# Yaarzo module guardrails

Map: `docs/DEVELOPMENT-GUARDRAILS.md`. Template: `docs/CURSOR-TASK-TEMPLATE.md`. Config: `scripts/guard/config.mjs`.

## Auto-detect TASK MODULE

At the start of every coding/editing task, infer the primary module from the request. If clear, do **not** ask the user to specify TASK MODULE.

Modules: HOMEPAGE, CUSTOM_PAGES, BLOG, FEED, CHATROOM, COMMUNITIES, POETRY, AUTH, GLOBAL_SEO, GLOBAL_SHELL, GUARDRAILS.

- Explicit `TASK MODULE:` in the prompt always wins (supported override).
- If ambiguous: name the ambiguity, do not start broad edits, ask **or** choose the smallest safe scope.

## Silent task-start (do not dump unless relevant)

Before edits, privately identify: module, ownership map, allowed files, protected files, do-not-touch modules, required regression tests.

## Smallest possible scope

Change **only** files for the detected module. No unrelated refactors, cleanup, renames, CSS, architecture, package updates, or generated files.

## Protected files

Do not edit unless the task cannot ship without them. Prefer a module-local fix. Before a broad shared change: explain why and list affected modules. After: that module’s `test:guard:*` plus golden smoke; report the protected change.

PROTECTED: `__root.tsx`, `$slug.tsx`, `$.tsx`, `public-routes.ts`, `auth-gate.tsx`, `app-settings.tsx`, `app-surface-css.ts`, `src/lib/seo/*`, `routeTree.gen.ts`, `src/styles.css`, `app-surfaces.css`, Supabase client/server/env/client-eager.

- Do not regenerate `routeTree.gen.ts` unless a route file was added/removed/renamed.
- Do not change AuthGate / `public-routes.ts` during SEO or content work.

## Isolation

- **CUSTOM_PAGES:** homepage/blog/feed/chatroom/perf must not alter `$slug` CMS routing/rendering/SEO/footer/sitemap eligibility unless this task is CUSTOM_PAGES or a proven shared regression. Sitemap published pages stay 200.
- **BLOG** is separate from Custom Pages. Homepage Community Blog uses the real Blog system (`/blog`).
- **Outside HOMEPAGE:** keep SSR crawlable `/`, one H1, SEO, real-data, Latest Signups, approved avatars, CMS footer, guest performance. Do not put app-surfaces CSS or heavy app providers on guest `/`.
- **FEED:** desktop 3-col grid + mobile bottom nav. **CHATROOM:** sidebar closed on mobile, always open on desktop.

## Gates

- Pre-commit: `npm run check:scope -- --module <detected-module>`. Review/remove accidental protected or cross-module edits.
- Pre-deploy: `npm run test:guard:<module>` (GUARDRAILS: `npm run guard:selfcheck`). If protected/shared changed: `npm run verify:predeploy`.
- Blockers: build fail, golden 5xx, sitemap 5xx/404, unknown slug 500, serious cross-module layout regression.
- Unrelated existing `tsc` debt is non-blocking unless `npm run build` fails. **Any 5xx blocks deploy.** Unknown slugs stay **404**, never 500.

## Final report (short)

TASK MODULE · files changed · protected yes/no · cross-module yes/no · guard tests · build · deployment · known regressions.

